    "intro": "A stage manager’s checklist says, “We fitted the latch, tied the cable and labelled the boxes.” None of the jobs is difficult to picture. Spelling the verbs is a different matter: *fit* doubles its final letter, *tie* drops part of its ending before *-ing*, and *label* has two accepted spelling patterns. Follow the checklist through a few changes of tense and number, then compare what happens when the choice depends on sound or clause type instead.",
    "exampleContext": "The manager updates a job from in progress to complete.",
