        "Listen to the next sound and read the next slot",
        "The manager puts the latch in *an envelope* and checks it with *a unit* from the tool kit. *Unit* begins with a consonant sound, so the spelling of the initial letter tells you too little. *An hour* illustrates the reverse: the written *h* is silent. Say the phrase aloud if the article is in doubt. When the manager asks “Aren’t I on the rota?”, that inverted form is widespread. In a statement the corresponding wording is *I’m not on the rota* or *I am not on the rota*. Some dialects use *amn’t*. The place where a form is available can be part of knowing its grammar, just as the previous chapter’s questions showed."
